  "issuedISO": "2026-11-10T08:42:00-10:00",
  "discussion": "A moderate, medium-period bump to northwest swell will fade later today and tonight. A much larger northwest to north-northwest swell generated by the dynamic fetch of a gale force low near Kamchatka will arrive on Wednesday and will bring at least advisory level surf to exposed north and west facing shores as it builds through the day and peaks Wednesday night. Surf will decrease to advisory levels on Thursday as the swell begins to fade and then fall below advisory levels by Friday. A northwest reinforcement is expected to arrive this weekend which could push surf back to advisory levels. Surf along east facing shores will increase for Wednesday as trade winds strengthen tonight. East shore surf remains elevated and choppy through Friday, then may diminish slightly this weekend. A small, long-period south swell may bring a small bump to south shore surf on Wednesday.",
